James sought guidance on revising a policy brief paragraph regarding adaptation investment benefits. A reviewer expressed concerns about claims of maximizing benefits due to the limited nature of the analysis. I advised James to avoid definitive language like “benefits are maximised” and suggested rephrasing it as “were largest in the modeled scenarios” instead. Key recommendations included: stating the limited scope before presenting numerical figures, potentially relocating investment multiples to a figure or annex, and exercising caution with claims of a “20-fold increase.” I provided a recommended revision emphasizing the substantial macroeconomic benefits while maintaining defensibility about the analysis's limitations. My preferred version balanced the findings on potential benefits with necessary qualifications around their implications.
